{"id":"b8","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":12,"of":17,"title":"The second binyan","titleHe":"בִּנְיַן פִּעֵל","goal":"Recognise and use pi'el, the pattern with a doubled middle letter.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Every Hebrew verb belongs to a binyan — a pattern the three root letters are poured into. You've been using פָּעַל all along. פִּעֵל is the second, and you can spot it: the present tense starts with מְ, and the middle root letter carries a dagesh."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פִּעֵל","en":"pi'el","note":"Often an intensified or causative sense; the middle root letter doubles.","verb":{"root":"ד־ב־ר","inf":"לְדַבֵּר","en":"to speak"},"tense":"present","rows":[{"label":"masculine singular","he":"","form":"מְדַבֵּר"},{"label":"feminine singular","he":"","form":"מְדַבֶּרֶת"},{"label":"masculine plural","he":"","form":"מְדַבְּרִים"},{"label":"feminine plural","he":"","form":"מְדַבְּרוֹת"}]},{"type":"binyan","he":"פִּעֵל","en":"pi'el","note":"Often an intensified or causative sense; the middle root letter doubles.","verb":{"root":"ד־ב־ר","inf":"לְדַבֵּר","en":"to speak"},"tense":"past","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"דִּבַּרְתִּי"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"דִּבַּרְתָּ"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"דִּבַּרְתְּ"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"דִּבֵּר"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"דִּבְּרָה"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"דִּבַּרְנוּ"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"דִּבַּרְתֶּם"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"דִּבַּרְתֶּן"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"דִּבְּרוּ"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Same root, different binyan, different meaning. From ל־מ־ד: לוֹמֵד in pa'al is learns, מְלַמֵּד in pi'el is teaches — makes someone learn."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מְדַבֵּר","en":"speaks","translit":"medaber"},{"he":"מְלַמֵּד","en":"teaches","translit":"melamed"},{"he":"מְסַפֵּר","en":"tells","translit":"mesaper"},{"he":"מְבַקֵּשׁ","en":"asks for","translit":"mevakesh"},{"he":"מ